@0    = ~Ye're crazy, Jai. Yer talkin' nonsense; I been there hundreds o' times, an' I never seen anythin' like that.~
@1    = ~I'm telling you, it's there. It has to be. I know every inch of this tower, and there's no way it could have gotten in otherwise.~
@2    = ~I been workin' here twenty-five years, boyo, don't ye think ye can tell me the lay o' the place!~
@3    = ~I'd wager I've done more watching down here than you, but no matter. If you won't listen to me, fine, let them invade. Then we'll see the right of it.~
@4    = ~Pfah! Balduran's Seatower be plenty secure. Don't ye be worryin' about that.~
@5    = ~Bloody younglings an' their bloody paranoia... a secret entrance? I think we'd of found it by now... Idjit...~
@6    = ~You don't look like guards. What do you think you're doing down here? We have a dangerous monster to restrain!~
@7    = ~I'm here to talk to a prisoner.~
@8    = ~Huh. Fancy that. We were just taking a walk above and bam, suddenly we're here! Where are we, exactly?~
@9    = ~What in the Nine Hells is that thing? Some kind of... fish-man?~
@10   = ~We were just leaving.~
@11   = ~Yes, how very... convenient. You are currently in the dungeons.~
@12   = ~Sahuagin. Dangerous aquatic creatures, prone to violence. Barbaric and uncivilized.~
@13   = ~We don't have time to waste. I need to chain this one up and report its appearance.~
@14   = ~This is a restricted area. You have no right to be here, so leave.~
@15   = ~Actually, I do. Here's a pass the Seatower commander gave me.~
@16   = ~Oh? Let me see the pass... Hmm, this is correct. You have permission to enter the prison and talk to the prisoners. I'll hand you the key, then. Be warned, though! The prisoners down here are very dangerous.~
@17   = ~That would be best.~
@18   = ~We will be watching you closely—for your own safety. It is dangerous down here. I suggest you leave before anything unsavory happens. I have been trained to deal with situations such as these.~
@19   = ~So have I. What were you saying about there being a way in earlier?~
@20   = ~We can look after ourselves. I'd like to talk to your prisoners.~
@21   = ~We'll just be leaving, then.~
@22   = ~If you must. Be quick.~
@23   = ~Let it be on your own head, then.~
@24   = ~Don't ye listen to his nonsense. He's no idea what he's talkin' about. These dungeons are perfectly safe.~
@25   = ~If they are perfectly safe, then why did I find a Sahuagin lurking in here?~
@26   = ~I know the sergeant already investigated the alcove. Fine, so behind the spore colony is just a dead end. I'm not saying the sergeant made a mistake, I'm saying the dungeons are bigger than that.~
@27   = ~Can ye be sure how long it's been down here? Could've come in from above a' night while we were doin' our rounds, it could!~
@28   = ~I've never run from a challenge before, I'm not about to start now.~
@29   = ~Be careful. The spore colony was obviously agitated by the sergeant investigating that corner. From the sounds of it, we're going to have to deal with some angry myconids again. It's high time we got rid of that spore colony, but I can't do so right away. Be careful when moving around.~
@30   = ~What just happened? I *told* you to be on your guard with the prisoners! The Amnian spy is gone—ah, she was a sly fox, that one. Nearly escaped us several times now. There won't be any repercussions for you, but be on your guard from now on! Hmph, now we have to report her missing.~
@31   = ~The Amnian spy is gone—ah, she was a sly fox, that one. Nearly escaped us several times now. Be on your guard around the prisoners! They'll make use of any trusting soul they can.~
@32   = ~The bandit managed to escape somehow. I can't prove anything, but I am sure you had something to do with this! I do wish you weren't down here, but there is nothing I can do against the commander's orders. Be done and be gone!~
@33   = ~Did you kill the bandit? Listen, the commander gave you access to the prison, this doesn't mean you can go around threatening the prisoners' lives! I do wish you weren't down here, but there is nothing I can do against the commander's orders. Be done and be gone!~
@34   = ~What happened back there with Sir Malastair? Ah, he shouldn't have gotten involved in intrigue if his heart can't take life in prison. I was afraid he'd die on us someday. I hope his mother won't give us any trouble.~
@35   = ~Who would've thought Sir Malastair was innocent all along! They just came and took him with them to bring him home.~
@36   = ~I overheard that it was you who freed him. Well done, I would say.~
@37   = ~You'd do best to leave this area. Who knows what else is down here?~
@38   = ~Reveal yourself, you filthy doppelganger scum!~
@39   = ~I'm afraid there is currently a lot going on. Your comrade was replaced by a doppelganger and they attacked the commander.~
@40   = ~The alcove behind the spore colony wasn't just a dead end. There's a whole cave and tunnel system back there!~
@41   = ~I found the body of a sergeant in the cave behind the breach... it bears the insignia of the commander's adjutant!~
@42   = ~I destroyed the spore colony, so it shouldn't give you any more trouble.~
@43   = ~There is a hole in the prison wall where the spore colony used to be.~
@44   = ~What were you saying about there being a way in earlier?~
@45   = ~What happened to the captured Sahuagin?~
@46   = ~We'll be fine. I'll have a look around.~
@47   = ~Dopp...?!~
@48   = ~Doppelganger scum? Why would I be... Wait. There were doppelgangers inside the tower?! The commander is aware, I presume—that's the reason you are down here!~
@49   = ~It all makes sense to me now... why my partner's accent would drop sometimes and how I caught him glaring at me, eyes full of malice, before he left... *shudder*~
@50   = ~Thank you for letting me know. I'll be sure to keep my eyes open. Er, and you, too. Maybe you're a doppelganger yourself? Maybe *I*'m one? I mean, I know I'm not, but... *sigh* Take care down here, will you?~
@51   = ~The creature went and died on us. I wasn't aware it couldn't survive out of the water for that long. Whatever the reason, it is dead now.~
@52   = ~What? You are telling me that you found the sergeant dead in a cave behind the prison wall? But... the last I saw him, he was walking right out of the prison door! How...~
@53   = ~My partner already went upstairs to report the breach in the wall. Something was odd, though... His accent slipped a couple of times and he had a strange look in his eyes... If you would go upstairs and make sure the commander is informed, I would appreciate it very much. I cannot leave my post, and it was just a gut feeling. I have no reason to distrust my partner.~
@54   = ~Yes, we noticed it after you left.~
@55   = ~*sigh* I hope *someone* tells me what is going on.~
@56   = ~It's doppelgangers, isn't it?~
@57   = ~Thanks! This will save us some trouble. We'll have it burned out. The last thing we need here is a myconid infestation.~
@58   = ~And it did show us that there is *indeed* a secret entrance... I hate it when I'm right.~
@59   = ~Yes, we know. One of the sergeants investigated it already, it's just a dead end, nothing more.~
@60   = ~Indeed. Thank you for reporting this to us. We'll make sure to pass the news on. Actually, I will pass it on now. Jai, you stay here—we can't leave the prison unguarded now, can we? This is important, yesss, it is.~
@61   = ~Indeed, this has to be reported right away... Wait, what just happened to his accent? And did you see that look in his eyes?... That's odd. I'll have to ask him about it when he gets back. Well, since one of us has to stay, I'll remain here on duty.~
@62   = ~Ye talk to Jai, I'm not a talker.~
